  "detail": "fallbackSetup() writes workers.setup_warning as soon as a worker reports a failed setup, before the local rerun has run. When the local setup also fails (the change itself broke setup, which the 'local setup failure blocks' test exercises), the worker is still flagged, so `limitless workers ls` blames a healthy worker. Issue #595 asks to show a setup MISMATCH: the worker's setup failed while the same request's setup passed locally. Nothing ever clears the warning either: not a later successful worker job, not a worker restart or reconnect, only revoking and re-pairing (INSERT OR REPLACE). So a worker whose environment was fixed stays flagged. Write the warning only after the local rerun's setup passes. Clear it when that worker next completes a job whose setup succeeds (or when it re-registers on a new release), and guard the clear so it doesn't erase a newer warning written meanwhile. Add tests: a local setup failure leaves the worker unflagged; a passing local rerun flags it; a later successful worker setup clears it."
 }
